   552	  # PLAN-194 W4.3 — RC TOOLCHAIN PROOF. RC tags never reach `publish`
   553	  # (its RC exclusion above is load-bearing and unchanged); they run
   554	  # THIS job instead, so the toolchain the GA publish will use is
   555	  # exercised before GA: the same Node line, the same exact npm, the
   556	  # same staging + install.sh trailer + packlist gate, then a
   557	  # `npm pack --dry-run` (no archive is written). Every step it shares
   558	  # with `publish` is a BYTE-IDENTICAL copy — edit both, or
   559	  # test_release_workflow_asserts.py (Plan194W4PublishToolchainTest)
   560	  # goes red. Its only own steps are an RC-aware VERSION check (an RC
   561	  # tree carries the GA VERSION — release.yml's RC flow) and the pack
   562	  # dry-run.
   563	  # Its permissions are `contents: read` ONLY: no OIDC token permission
