   320	## Effort
   321	
   322	Levels and defaults depend on the model: see the effort table in the Claude
   323	Code model-configuration docs (some models have no `xhigh`, and a model
   324	missing from that table does not support effort at all).
   325	
   326	- **Claude Opus 5.5 defaults to `medium`**; the other models that support
   327	  effort default to `high`, except Opus 4.7 (`xhigh`) and, for your
   328	  organization's default model, the effort level your organization sets
   329	  (docs, read 2026-09-22). Probe E5, with no effort set anywhere, read
   330	  `medium` applied to `claude-opus-5-5`. If you relied on the old default,
   331	  set it explicitly. The model catalog in the Claude Code 2.1.295 binary
   332	  (read 2026-10-09) also gives `medium` to Sonnet 5.5 and Haiku 5.5, and
   333	  `high` to Fable 5.1.
   334	- The `effortLevel` settings key (top level, or per model under
   335	  `modelSettings.<model>.effortLevel`) accepts only `low` to `xhigh`; a `max`
   336	  value there is dropped. In the 2.1.295 binary both schemas still list
   337	  `low` to `xhigh` and drop any other value (read 2026-10-09).
   338	- **An `xhigh` in a settings file needs a Claude Code that accepts it.** The
   339	  changelog (read 2026-09-23) adds the `xhigh` level in 2.1.111. Two later
   340	  entries show one failure shape, a single value a build does not accept
   341	  costing the whole file: 2.1.121 fixes "invalid legacy enum values in
   342	  `settings.json` invalidating the entire settings file", and 2.1.281 notes
   343	  that older CLI versions skip a settings file holding
   344	  `"attribution": false`. A skipped `.claude/settings.json` takes every
   345	  hook it registers with it, the framework's governance hooks included.
   346	  Neither entry names `effortLevel` and no older build was run for this
   347	  page, so which builds skip a file for `effortLevel: "xhigh"` is not
   348	  measured; builds before 2.1.111 do not have the level at all. The framework's
   349	  v1.4.2 release (planned; not tagged on 2026-09-24) ships
   350	  `effortLevel: "xhigh"` in a fresh install's settings and names Claude
   351	  Code 2.1.280, the Opus 5.5 floor, as its minimum. Run `claude --version`
   352	  before you set `xhigh` in any settings file yourself.
   353	- A top-level `effortLevel` in your **user** settings is ignored for Opus 5.5
   354	  and models released after it.
   355	  In project, local or `--settings` sources it applies to every model.
   356	- `max` persists only through the `CLAUDE_CODE_EFFORT_LEVEL` environment
   357	  variable, which takes precedence over `--effort`, `/effort` and the effort
   358	  settings, `ultracode` included; a `maxEffortLevel` cap still applies
   359	  (docs). Probe E7 (Claude Code 2.1.280;
   360	  `CLAUDE_CODE_EFFORT_LEVEL=max` plus `ultracode: true`) saw every tool call
   361	  run at `max`, including one from a workflow agent started with
   362	  `{effort: 'low'}`.
   363	
   364	**On Claude Code 2.1.280, `ultracode` and `max` did not combine.** There,
   365	`ultracode: true` made the default effort `xhigh` and enabled dynamic
   366	workflow orchestration. The Claude Code
   367	docs (model configuration, read 2026-09-22) name three conditions under which
   368	it is not available: workflows are turned off, the model does not support
   369	`xhigh`, or an effort cap below `xhigh` applies to the model. That cap is an
   370	organization limit or a `maxEffortLevel` in any settings file; when several
   371	set one, the lowest applies (settings reference). The 2.1.280 binary's own
   372	description of the key calls it session-scoped, "typically provided via
   373	--settings or the apply_flag_settings control request"; the published
   374	settings reference gives it the scope "Any file", and the local-file probe in
   375	step 3 applied it. When the resolved effort is not `xhigh`, the flag stays
   376	set but has no effect. Probes E3, E4, E7 and E8 (`ultracode: true` through
   377	`--settings`, with `CLAUDE_CODE_EFFORT_LEVEL=max` or `--effort max`) read
   378	`ultracode` set in the settings but not applied (`get_settings`
   379	`applied.ultracode` false), while E1 and E6 (without `max`) read it applied.
   380	`/effort max` was not probed. The lifted subagent limit and the Auto-mode
   381	consent skip belong to an applied `ultracode` (docs); neither was probed on
   382	its own.
   383	
   384	The 2.1.284 changelog says Ultracode "no longer forces xhigh effort and stays
   385	on at any effort level". The 2.1.295 binary's description of the key (read
   386	2026-10-09) keeps the session-scoped text, says that interactive toggles
   387	never persist it, and names two requirements: workflows enabled and a model
   388	that supports ultracode. It names no effort condition. None of the probes
   389	above was re-run on 2.1.295, so whether `ultracode` and `max` combine there
   390	is not measured.
   391	
   392	The combination recommended here is `ultracode: true` for the main session,
   393	with `max` requested per agent inside workflow scripts
   394	(`agent(prompt, {effort: 'max'})`). Probe E6 (Claude Code 2.1.280) measured
   395	it with `ultracode` passed through `--settings`: `ultracode` applied, the
   396	main session and a subagent ran at `xhigh`, and a workflow agent started
   397	with `{effort: 'max'}` ran at `max` (one started with `{effort: 'low'}` ran
   398	at `low`). A local-file `ultracode` was probed only for the applied setting
   399	(step 3), not for per-agent effort.
