   223	## 4. The SPEC contract
   224	
   225	`SPEC/v1/` is the published, versioned compliance contract (SemVer; currently
   226	v1.4.3, aligned with the repo `VERSION`). It contains 28 schema files defining
   227	the stable interfaces an adopter can pin to — among them `audit-log.schema.md`,
   228	`hook-io.schema.md`, `plan.schema.md`, `debate.schema.md`,
   229	`skill-frontmatter.schema.md`, `tier-policy.schema.md`, and
   230	`install-cli.md` (which versions the `install.sh` CLI flags as an API).
   231	
   232	The SPEC matters because it separates *what the framework promises* from *how
   233	this repository happens to implement it today*. An install pins a SPEC version;
   234	internal refactors that keep the schemas stable do not break adopters.
   235	
   236	Decisions that shape these contracts are recorded as Architecture Decision
